WEBVTT

1
00:00:10.334 --> 00:00:17.078
After seeing the freshly painted fence, Aunt Polly decided to let Tom play outdoors for the rest of the afternoon.

2
00:00:17.079 --> 00:00:22.880
The first thing Tom wanted to do was get revenge on Sid for telling Aunt Polly about his collar.

3
00:00:22.881 --> 00:00:28.516
So Tom waited by the fence and ambushed his half brother with balls made of dried-up mud.

4
00:00:28.517 --> 00:00:34.275
Before Aunt Polly could rush to Sid's rescue, Tom managed to hit him with six or seven balls.

5
00:00:34.276 --> 00:00:41.581
Sid screamed in fear and pain.Then Tom jumped over the fence and was gone.

6
00:00:41.582 --> 00:00:48.891
When Tom arrived at the town square a few minutes later, a group of boys was already there, ready to play army games.

7
00:00:48.892 --> 00:00:56.827
Tom and his best friend, Joe Harper, were appointed as generals, and they commanded their armies all afternoon.

8
00:00:56.828 --> 00:01:04.547
As the sun began to set, the boys counted their "dead" and "wounded," and it was determined that Tom had won a great battle.

9
00:01:04.548 --> 00:01:09.225
Joe and Tom shook hands and agreed to meet next Saturday for another battle.

10
00:01:09.226 --> 00:01:12.764
On his way home, Tom spied a new girl.

11
00:01:12.765 --> 00:01:18.475
He thought the new girl was lovely, with blue eyes and braided blond hair.

12
00:01:18.476 --> 00:01:24.510
At the sight of this new angel, the love Tom had pledged to a girl named Amy Lawrence instantly vanished.

13
00:01:24.511 --> 00:01:27.648
Tom soon began to show off for the new girl.

14
00:01:27.649 --> 00:01:34.040
He balanced a stick on his nose, and he walked up and down the street where they both lived.

15
00:01:34.041 --> 00:01:38.920
When the girl reached her house, she halted and looked over at Tom for only a second.

16
00:01:38.921 --> 00:01:41.214
But it was enough to encourage Tom.

17
00:01:41.215 --> 00:01:46.671
After she went inside, Tom lingered near her house, hoping to see her one more time.

18
00:01:46.672 --> 00:01:50.044
But the pretty new girl never reappeared.

19
00:01:50.045 --> 00:01:54.035
Still, Tom returned home in high spirits.

20
00:01:54.036 --> 00:01:58.634
His aunt scolded him for throwing mud balls at Sid, but Tom didn't care.

21
00:01:58.635 --> 00:02:03.100
When his aunt hit him for stealing sugar from the sugar bowl, Tom didn't care.

22
00:02:03.101 --> 00:02:08.040
He just smiled and said, "You never hit Sid when he takes sugar."

23
00:02:08.041 --> 00:02:13.004
"Sid doesn't torment me the way you do," she reminded him.

24
00:02:13.005 --> 00:02:16.725
That night Tom went to bed with the new girl on his mind.

25
00:02:16.726 --> 00:02:20.289
He was determined to devise a way to get her to notice him.

26
00:02:20.290 --> 00:02:24.756
The next morning Aunt Polly forced Tom to put on his Sunday suit for church.

27
00:02:24.757 --> 00:02:31.775
After a quick breakfast, she escorted Tom to church to make sure he attended Sunday school.

28
00:02:31.776 --> 00:02:38.713
The day's lesson consisted of memorizing five verses of the Bible, but Tom was having a problem concentrating.

29
00:02:38.714 --> 00:02:45.807
At last the lesson ended, and Tom and the other students had a fifteen-minute break before the church service began.

30
00:02:45.808 --> 00:02:53.542
Although Tom had not bothered to memorize the five verses, he had finally devised a plan to make the new girl interested in him.

31
00:02:53.543 --> 00:03:01.688
The other children had paid Tom to let them paint, so now his pockets overflowed with marbles, candies, fishhooks, and other goodies.

32
00:03:01.689 --> 00:03:07.590
Tom decided to use his new wealth to buy "verse recitation" tickets.

33
00:03:07.591 --> 00:03:12.292
These tickets were rewards for students who correctly recited verses from the Bible.

34
00:03:12.293 --> 00:03:17.140
For every two lines of verse correctly recited, students were given one blue ticket.

35
00:03:17.141 --> 00:03:22.590
Ten blue tickets equaled one red ticket; ten red tickets equaled one yellow ticket.

36
00:03:22.591 --> 00:03:26.167
For ten yellow tickets, a student could earn a Bible.

37
00:03:26.168 --> 00:03:30.059
A Bible for reciting two thousand lines of verse!

38
00:03:30.060 --> 00:03:35.430
Only older students were able to earn a Bible because it took years of saving tickets.

39
00:03:35.431 --> 00:03:39.328
Tom didn't want a Bible, but he did want to win the new girl's heart.

40
00:03:39.329 --> 00:03:44.311
To win her heart, he had decided that he must seem like a better person than the other boys.

41
00:03:44.312 --> 00:03:49.359
In church, the moment to impress the new girl finally came.

42
00:03:49.360 --> 00:03:54.082
First the minister asked all the smartest and most studious children how many tickets they had.

43
00:03:54.083 --> 00:03:56.752
None of them had enough for a Bible yet.

44
00:03:56.753 --> 00:04:01.158
"Does anyone have enough tickets for a Bible?" asked the minister.

45
00:04:01.159 --> 00:04:03.857
To the shock of everyone, Tom stood up.

46
00:04:03.858 --> 00:04:09.897
Then he proudly marched forward to bring his tickets to the minister.
